  "overview": {
    "implementation_summary": "The codebase implements a 3D multimodal large language model (PointLLM/GreenPLM) that integrates PointNet++ based point cloud encoders with a LLaVA-style language model architecture. The system processes 3D point cloud data through a hierarchical encoder (PointNet2ClassificationSSG, PointcloudEncoder), projects features into the LLM's embedding space via a shared projector (Encoder), and handles multimodal training tokens through specialized data collators (DataCollatorForPointTextDataset). The implementation includes PyTorch Lightning training loops with custom trainers (LLaVATrainer) and supports staged training workflows with frozen backbone strategies.",
    "architecture_summary": "The architecture follows an encoder-projector-LLM pattern: (1) Point cloud encoder using PointNet++ SA modules (PointnetSAModuleMSG, Group, QueryAndGroup) for local-to-global feature aggregation; (2) Shared projection layer (Encoder/PointcloudEncoder) mapping from encoder space to LLM hidden space with patch dropout and skeleton grouping; (3) LLaVA-based language model (LlavaMetaModel) consuming projected point tokens injected into the language token stream. Auxiliary components include BNMomentumScheduler for batch norm management and PointnetFPModule for feature propagation.",
    "training_summary": "Training follows a three-stage curriculum: Stage I (Text-First Interface Warmup) establishes projector-language coupling with frozen backbones; Stage II (Rich Instruction Alignment) expands to complex dialog patterns; Stage III (Point-Language Transfer) activates 3D point cloud inputs with compact token aggregation. The training loop uses Adam optimizer with learning rate scheduling, cross-entropy loss for classification, and supports custom data loaders for point-text datasets (ObjectPointCloudDataset, CustomDataset). Checkpoint behavior is managed through LLaVATrainer.",
    "alignment_summary": "Overall alignment score is 0.44 with 100% module coverage (7/7 found) but partial pipeline coverage (75%, 3/4 steps) and no explicit loss implementations documented. High confidence alignments (1.0) exist for TrainingArguments (M1) and shared projector Encoder (M6). Medium confidence (0.5-0.6) for point feature injection (M2), data loading (M3), token conversion (M4), and aggregation (M5). Low confidence (0.4) for trainer checkpoint behavior (M7). Stage II pipeline step lacks code evidence. Manual verification recommended for point cloud encoder integration specifics."
  },
